[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Pawn Game"]
[Variation "Queen's Pawn Game: Zukertort Variation, 3.Nc3"]
[ECO "D02"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "qgd-setup,c5-break,transposition"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "2.Nf3 Nf6 3.Nc3 or 3.c4"]
[Start "london-main 2...Nf6"]

3. Nc3 { The knight blocks the c-pawn, so White gives up the c4 break and aims for e4 instead. } ( 3. c4 { Now it is a Queen's Gambit. } 3... e6 { The Queen's Gambit Declined set-up: the pawn on e6 holds d5. After 4.Nc3 Be7 it is the Three Knights Variation, taught in the Queen's Gambit Declined course. } ) 3... e6 { Holds d5 with a pawn and opens the bishop on f8. Black plays the usual set-up: ...Be7, ...O-O and ...c5. } 4. Bg5 ( 4. Bf4 Be7 5. e3 O-O 6. Bd3 c5 { Hits d4 now that the bishop on f4 no longer guards it. } ) ( 4. e3 Be7 5. Bd3 O-O 6. O-O c5 { The freeing break: the knight on c3 cannot defend d4, and the c-file opens for Black's rook. } ) 4... Be7 5. e3 ( 5. Bxf6 Bxf6 6. e4 O-O { Castles before the centre opens. If e5, the bishop simply goes back to e7 and ...c5 hits the pawn chain. } 7. e5 Be7 ) 5... O-O 6. Bd3 c5 { Strikes at d4. With the knight on c3, White has no pawn on c3 to support the centre. } 7. O-O b6 { Prepares ...Bb7, and if White takes on c5, the b-pawn recaptures and keeps a pawn in the centre. Plan: ...Bb7, ...Nbd7 or ...Nc6, and ...Rc8. } *
